  "limitations": [
    "Five small public tasks run once per workflow and one small third-party repository task run twice per workflow; this is not a general coding benchmark or an industry ranking.",
    "The explicitly requested two-child integration demonstrates lifecycle, collection and acceptance, not autonomous delegation choice or multi-agent quality gains.",
    "Every run is retained, including failures; no competitor baseline or statistical claim is made.",
    "The initial four repository runs used a flawed ambient-type oracle and exposed an Extend routing defect. Their raw failures are retained separately; corrected runs must not be merged into a single unchanged-protocol score.",
    "The small suite and explicit collaboration case preceded the final Extend routing correction; evaluator fingerprints distinguish the runtime versions.",
    "The third-party repository has fixed direct test dependency versions but no upstream lockfile; transitive resolution is not fully pinned.",
    "Small-suite latency includes setup; repository execution time is separated from setup. Background local acceptance work overlapped with some small runs, so timings are descriptive only.",
    "Cumulative tokens include repeated input and cache reads, plus child usage where present; they are not the context-window size.",
    "Model prices were not configured. Cost is unknown, never reported as free.",
    "This allowlisted aggregate excludes provider URLs, credentials, local paths, session IDs and raw transcripts."
